      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Biomass briquettes are a biofuel substitute made of biodegradable green waste with lower emissions of greenhouses gases and carbon dioxide than traditional fuel sources. They are used for heating, cooking fuel, and electricity generation, usually in developing countries. The energy content of briquettes ranges from 4.48 to 5.95 kilojoule per gram (kJ/g) depending on composition. Biomass briquette fuel is a renewable energy source made from biomass materials such as agricultural and forestry residues.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "生物质煤是一种由可生物降解的绿色废物制成的生物燃料替代品，其温室气体和二氧化碳的排放量低于传统燃料来源。它们通常用于供暖，烹饪燃料和发电，通常在发展中国家。根据组成，煤砖的能量含量范围从每克4.48到5.95千焦耳（kJ/g）。生物质煤燃料是一种由农业和林业残留物等生物质材料制成的可再生能源。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
